rFor is built-in type m's slot for the special method name, or nil."] [282 3 "// METH_COEXIST (queue 290): the method its type defines beside the slot, a method_descriptor"] [283 3 "// (frozenset.__contains__ bound is a builtin_function_or_method: keyword.iskeyword)"] [284 3 "// objectDescr: bound to the instance itself, as the slot wrapper was (a dict subclass's __missing__:"] [285 3 "// urllib.parse's _Quoter(dict).__getitem__)"] [294 1 "// coexistMethods are the built-in types' METH_COEXIST methods (dict_methods', list_methods', set_methods' and"] [295 1 "// frozenset_methods' __getitem__ and __contains__): method descriptors where the other slots have slot wrappers."] [315 5 "// object's own slots take the instance itself, not a built-in subclass's value: object.__str__ of an"] [316 5 "// int subclass is repr(self), its class's __repr__ (queue 287: test_enum's __str__ = object.__str__)"] [320 5 "// set_repr names a subclass's type (Py_TYPE): set.__repr__(sub) is \"sub({...})\" (py-core-1124: test_pprint's"] [321 5 "// test_set_reprs)"] [327 2 "// the number protocol's binary methods (__add__, __radd__, __iadd__ ...): the Binary, RBinary and InPlace"] [328 2 "// slots, NotImplemented when they do not apply (PY6h's REQUEST, queue 200: test_asyncio reads int.__add__)"] [353 6 "// wrap_ternaryfunc_r: the operands swapped, the modulus third"] [366 22 "// wrap_indexargfunc"] [377 4 "// object_str: tp_repr, never the type's own __str__ (REQUEST of PY6g for PY6-core: a class with"] [378 4 "// __str__ = object.__str__, doctest's DocTestCase, recursed without end)"] [499 5 "// dict_subscript sees self's type: a subclass's d.__getitem__(k) calls its __missing__ as d[k] does"] [500 5 "// (queue 202: urllib.parse's _Quoter(safe).__getitem__ raised KeyError: test_http_cookies,"] [501 5 "// test_wsgiref's request_uri)"] [609 3 "// one object per type, so that object.__new__ is object.__new__ (enum's _find_new_ compares them;"] [610 3 "// PY5e, part 2b)"] [614 3 "// tp_new_wrap